Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 16:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] llvm-libgcc: make builtins install path relative

get_compiler_rt_install_dir can return an absolute path when
COMPILER_RT_INSTALL_PATH is absolute.  llvm-libgcc subsequently prefixes that
path with LLVM_LIBGCC_INSTALL_LIBRARY_DIR, installing a duplicate library below
/usr/lib/usr/lib.  It also uses the absolute path as the target of libgcc.a;
that symlink escapes a recipe sysroot and is therefore broken for dependent
recipes such as gcc-runtime.

Express an absolute compiler-rt path relative to the directory containing the
libgcc compatibility symlinks.  This installs the builtins archive once at the
expected location and keeps libgcc.a valid both in the image and in recipe
sysroots.

Upstream-Status: Pending

---
 llvm-libgcc/CMakeLists.txt | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/llvm-libgcc/CMakeLists.txt b/llvm-libgcc/CMakeLists.txt
index dc779170529d..ea6628ac42aa 100644
--- a/llvm-libgcc/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/llvm-libgcc/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -131,2 +131,10 @@ get_compiler_rt_install_dir(${COMPILER_RT_DEFAULT_TARGET_ARCH} install_dir_built
-# Drop a leading "lib/" if present so we don't duplicate lib/lib
-string(REGEX REPLACE "^lib/" "" install_dir_builtins "${install_dir_builtins}")
+# Keep this relative to the directory where the libgcc compatibility symlinks
+# are installed.  An absolute COMPILER_RT_INSTALL_PATH must not become either
+# lib//usr/lib/... during installation or an absolute symlink target.
+if (IS_ABSOLUTE "${install_dir_builtins}")
+  file(RELATIVE_PATH install_dir_builtins
+    "${CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX}/${LLVM_LIBGCC_INSTALL_LIBRARY_DIR}"
+    "${install_dir_builtins}")
+else()
+  string(REGEX REPLACE "^lib/" "" install_dir_builtins "${install_dir_builtins}")
+endif()
--
2.51.0
